:[5566618546,5566651972,5566713561,5577451717,5578038543,5578376761,5580015794,5580024701,5580039812,5580084717,5580599974,5580641996,5580930133],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nAn unresolved asynchronous-completion defect and cross-version cancellation behavior require correction and final human review.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 previously missed issue</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Handle async query overloads with a null failure consumer</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200binfluxdb-2.4/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200binfluxdb/\u200bv2_4/\u200bInfluxDbImplInstrumentation.java:110`\n\n[Javaagent] `query(query, successConsumer, null)` is misclassified as synchronous because argument 2 is the failure consumer. In the tested 2.14 client, this overload still enqueues the request and delivers successful responses to argument 1. Method-exit advice therefore ends the span and duration before the response arrives, preventing later statement errors or success-callback failures from updating them. Recognize the success consumer at argument 1 as well, and add a delayed-response regression with a null failure consumer.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5580930133","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5580930133}],"frozen_at":1792472706,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-20T05:05:06Z","frozen_sha":"91669ba1f1a6e3d1d21297a08823c5269c56c6c5","head_ref":"copilot/split-20685-influxdb","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":39363887052},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nSplits the InfluxDB changes from #20685, correcting query outcomes and duration timing without changing other integrations.\n\n- **Error classification:** Classify HTTP-200 top-level and per-statement errors with bounded `error.type`, never raw error text. Retain available HTTP error codes.\n- **Terminal completion:** End asynchronous and chunked operations exactly once after callbacks and chunk processing finish, retaining callback, transport, and decoding failures, including newer-client decoding failures without a failure consumer.\n- **Cancellation and compatibility:** Make the call available before failure consumers run so pre-response cancellation remains successful. Preserve `DONE` handling, callback parent context, and supported 2.4 APIs.\n- **Regression coverage:** Cover synchronous response errors, one asynchronous statement error, successful and failed chunked completion, cancellation before and after response delivery, callback failures after cancellation, and a single 2.4 statement-error case, with span and duration-metric assertions. Retain HTTP `400` assertions in the existing failing-query integration test.","title":"Fix InfluxDB query error classification and async completion"},"mode":"publish","pr":20703,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792466522,"generation":6,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"b80041c4df3c4d05a0856e28fcb1d087","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"8a303e536ff24a63b84e43f7e1553195","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81","workflow_revision":"702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":null,"id":39373120161,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/39373120161"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":["ba399cd50d4866adb07072f29b61398f3d6e5dde968bc184347f0cd7dfcbe6f3","923bf8bd6de9ad7c27de3757551e84f7c9c32b5740465b377713e2e37f7ee7e1","547b8f129a939d6ff1189ede2d3380403c1fa7d93201ae1402ad6e6fb8ed6d21"],"seen_inline_findings":["3e32339eb44fd53c4286b907aca8d9f003c39de16d6c00a69ffe24cae710b032"],"seen_missed_findings":["3b92ac1ee2eaeb298af638d69cb0a3fc9c4d349dfd9c793f6bf8d94da9b68a8d","a524e97df7146e1033d95fbc23adf16ce420477f9f8d01eb19ec4fada9eee70a"],"stage":"running"}